  "conclusion": "Fixing the initial symmetric chemical conductances while retaining changing volumes and dilution restores sustained chemical formation in both existing histories 7 and 8. Removing dilution alone does not restore formation. The same qualified rescue pattern identifies a shared tested contribution of conductance remodeling, not a unique universal cause, full moving-system stability, biological identity, fresh carry development or general transport closure.",
